//   participles as attributes (kehtiv pakkumine, automaatselt pikenev tellimus, makstud summa, tagastatav) — taught in 052
//     (notice, transformation; terms text, word forms), back in 053–054 (complaint, terms);
//   the impersonal in terms and conditions and the conditional in complaints (pikendatakse, ei tagastata; paluksin,
//     oleksin tänulik, oleksin valinud) — taught in 053 (dialogue, notice, rule table; error correction, word order),
//     used in 054's complaint letter (transformation with the past conditional).
// Final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 11): 051 KUUL L→W, 052 PROB L→S, 053 LUGU R→W, 054 AVAS R→S,
// 055 EKS. Exam corners (one Harno B2 task a teaching lesson): 051 L1 (ten short announcements, played once), 052 S2
// (argument cards on free trials), 053 R2b (consumer-rights Q&A, short answers), 054 W2b (argument on investing savings).
// Main Kasuta tasks: 051 W13 letter to the supplier, 052 S04 phone negotiation with the ad seller, 053 W08 reply to the
// shop's letter, 054 S16 budget presentation at the bank. The exam 055 has four timed parts (PART).
// Module 10's words return (≥ 30 %): konflikt, tüli, pinge, kompromiss, kokkulepe, järeleandmine, tingimus,
